# Fledge Alpha — findings by Big Pickle

> **SELF-EXCLUDED (notes only, not scored).** Fledge Alpha is a real, heavily used model —
> 179B tokens and ~107,000 completed sessions on OpenCode Zen in its first two days — but it
> has **no identified lab, no official specs, no vendor benchmark and no independent
> evaluation**. The only public numbers about its quality come from one user's ad-hoc checks
> whose own write-up says they do not support a model review or quality ranking. Per
> `model-report-TEMPLATE.md` (SELF-EXCLUSION) and `RULES.md`, this is saved as
> `Big_Pickle.md.excluded` instead of a scored `.md`, so no pseudo-benchmark enters the
> dataset mean.

- Source: OpenCode Zen / unattributed lab (`opencode/fledge-alpha-free`, `opencode/fledge-alpha`)
- Date: 2026-10-02 (UTC)
- Overview and scoring methodology: `../../model-comparison.md`
- Cross-model signed log: `../../model-findings.md`

## Model card

- **Name:** Fledge Alpha (tier: `fledge-alpha-free`)
- **Short description:** An unidentified model that appeared on OpenCode Zen in stealth mode
  around 2026-10-01 and immediately drew heavy agentic traffic. It is served free
  (subscription-plan pricing) with a 1M-token context and a reasoning toggle. Nobody — not
  OpenCode, not the vendor, not the trackers — will say who builds it or what sits underneath.
- **Provider / access:** OpenCode Zen, `opencode/fledge-alpha-free` (the free tier entry) and
  `opencode/fledge-alpha` in OpenCode's usage data. Served via the Zen Responses endpoint.
- **Release / knowledge:** 2026-10-01 (Zen catalogue date). No knowledge cutoff published.
- **IDs:** `fledge-alpha-free`, `fledge-alpha` on Zen. No vendor model-ID string exists.
- **Context window:** 1,048,576 tokens total, 131,072 max output (models.dev / modelcompare.dev
  metadata). This folder covers the base model; the `-free` suffix is a pricing tier, not a
  different model.
- **Modalities:** text in/out. models.dev marks **attachments unsupported**, so it is treated as
  text-only for scoring purposes. Reasoning: yes, with `low` / `high` / `max` effort modes.
  Tool calling: yes. Structured/JSON mode: not reported.
- **Pricing (as of 2026-10-02):** **$0 in / $0 out** — subscription-plan pricing on Zen, $0.0000
  average cost per session, $0 total recorded spend. No paid tier is documented.
- **Architecture:** proprietary, not open weights. Parameter count, MoE/dense structure and
  training data are all unknown.

